<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maratha Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marathas, Maratha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maratha Empire was an Indian state founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> in the seventeenth century in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. Its long war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> drained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, and in the eighteenth century the Marathas became the dominant power in much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Defeat at Panipat in 1761 and wars with the British led to its final collapse in 1818.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maratha-empire.jpg" alt="Maratha Empire" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India1760_1905.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
